#===============================================================================
#  ARDHANARISHVARA OS — ENGINEERING SUPPORT DOCUMENT
#  SovereignOS Kernel Debugger
#  File: kernel_debugger.support
#===============================================================================
#  PURPOSE:
#    Engineering reference for the SovereignOS kernel debugger responsible for:
#      • breakpoint handling
#      • stack trace capture
#      • memory inspection
#      • debug event logging
#
#===============================================================================
#  MODULE SUMMARY:
#
#    - [Breakpoints](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Breakpoints)
#    - [Stack Tracing](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Stack_Tracing)
#    - [Memory Inspection](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Memory_Inspection)
#    - [Debug Logging](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Debug_Logging)
#    - [Debugger Snapshot](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Debugger_Snapshot)
#
#===============================================================================
#  FUNCTION OVERVIEW:
#
#    - register_breakpoint(name, handler)
#         Registers a breakpoint.
#
#    - trigger(name, context)
#         Triggers breakpoint handler.
#
#    - register_memory_hook(name, handler)
#         Registers memory inspection hook.
#
#    - inspect(hook, payload)
#         Executes memory inspection.
#
#    - snapshot()
#         Returns debugger state.
#
#===============================================================================
#  BREAKPOINT STRUCTURE FORMAT:
#
#    {
#      "id": "BRK-XXXX",
#      "name": "scheduler.tick",
#      "handler": <async callable>,
#      "timestamp": <epoch>
#    }
#
